From afd1c882398e322287c26ab3e677ab71a40194e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mlgprorektm8 <67933lance@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:40:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Native renderer (experimental, launcher option "Renderer")

The native renderer: GT Sport's command buffers decoded and recorded straight into Vulkan by a
NativeRenderer with its own image registry, instead of shadGT's renderer. Chosen with the
launcher's "Renderer" dropdown (GPU.native_renderer); RYGT_NATIVE=1 or =0 overrides it. The
old renderer stays the default.

- Races, menus and car screens render as with the old renderer (FIX-150 rain drops, FIX-153
  remapped car memory, FIX-154 car selection screens and shared targets, FIX-156 first clear
  of new depth buffers (Tokyo's track map), FIX-157 GPU-baked pictures kept while their memory
  is untouched (light probes)); about 33-39 fps in the Tokyo rain benchmark against 29.
- Known open problems: in Tokyo at night the cockpit's ambient light flickers between warm and
  dark frames (the cockpit's environment cube is built too dark on some frames); rare frames
  drawn from a wrong camera.
- Diagnostics (all opt-in): frame dumps (RYGT_FRAME_DUMP_AT, several times; _ON_FILL,
  _ON_STORE, _ALL_TEXTURES, _EXPOSURE), RYGT_NATIVE_WATCH_TEXTURE (several addresses; probe
  read-backs, bind/write/evict/link logs), RYGT_TRACE_RANGE, RYGT_PEEK, RYGT_EXPOSURE_LOG,
  RYGT_NATIVE_HOLD_COMPUTE, RYGT_NATIVE_SHARED_TARGETS=0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
